Serve OpenMAIC under a reverse-proxy subpath

Next generates every /_next/ asset URL from basePath, so without it an app
served under a path prefix 404s on its own chunks. OpenMAIC has no basePath, so
this adds one, read from NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH and normalised to undefined when
empty — Next rejects '' but an unset variable reads as ''. A no-op for anyone
serving the app at a domain root, which is every deployment that does not need
this.

Needed only for the same-origin embed. Verified: with NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH set,
the app serves under /maic-app and its Link headers preload
/maic-app/_next/static/... correctly.

What basePath does NOT fix, and what makes the same-origin shape harder than it
looks — see deploy/OPENMAIC_EMBED.md:

- `fetch('/api/...')` is not router-aware and keeps no prefix. OpenMAIC makes 53
  such calls from the browser with no central helper to patch, so on a shared
  origin they land on whatever else owns /api there.
- Raw /public references (/logo-horizontal.png, /avatars/*.png) are likewise
  unprefixed, the same gap this fork documents for itself in web/lib/basePath.ts.

Both have to be resolved by the reverse proxy, not by this patch.

diff --git a/next.config.ts b/next.config.ts
index 1493e7b5..1c9f54fe 100644
--- a/next.config.ts
+++ b/next.config.ts
@@ -1,6 +1,16 @@
 import type { NextConfig } from 'next';
 
 const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
+  // Subpath this app is served under when a reverse proxy routes a prefix to it
+  // (e.g. nginx `location /maic-app` -> this container), or unset when it owns
+  // the domain root. Next cannot serve a subpath without it: every /_next/ asset
+  // URL is generated from this, so without it the framed app 404s on its own
+  // chunks.
+  //
+  // Structural, so it has to be baked at build time rather than read per
+  // request. Empty string is normalised to undefined because Next rejects '' but
+  // an unset env var reads as ''.
+  basePath: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH || undefined,
   output: process.env.VERCEL ? undefined : 'standalone',
   outputFileTracingIncludes: {
